# Git commands after updates

When you finish a task that changed project files, end the response with a **Deploy** section containing copy-paste git commands.

## Required format

```bash
cd ~/Projects/trenddrop
git add .
git commit -m "Short summary of what changed"
git push origin main
```

- Write a clear, specific commit message (not "update" or "fix").
- Mention Railway will auto-redeploy if the repo is connected.
- Do **not** run commit/push unless the user explicitly asks — only show the commands.
- Skip this section for question-only replies with no file changes.

## Optional follow-up

If env vars or admin actions are needed after deploy, list them after the git block.
